# The same two jobs as the systemd timers, for a host without systemd.
#
#   sudo crontab -u root deploy/crontab.example
#
# Use one or the other, never both: two backups at 02:00 writing to the same
# directory is twice the disk and one of them pruning sets the other just made.
#
# WHAT CRON DOES WORSE THAN THE TIMERS, SO YOU KNOW WHAT YOU ARE CHOOSING
#
#   · A missed run is simply missed. The systemd timer has Persistent=true and
#     runs a backup the host was switched off for; cron does not.
#   · Failure handling is MAILTO, which needs a working MTA on the box. The
#     timers call deploy/alert.sh on failure, which needs one URL.
#   · Nothing stops two runs overlapping if one is slow. `flock` below does.
#
# Set MAILTO to somebody who reads it, or the exit codes go nowhere — which is
# the normal way a backup is discovered to have been failing for three weeks.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
MAILTO=CHANGE-ME@example.com

# ── nightly backup, 02:00, database and objects together ───────────────────
# flock so a slow night cannot overlap the next one. The exit code reaches cron,
# which mails MAILTO; the JSON line goes to the journal via logger so a shipper
# can pick it up.
0 2 * * * cd /srv/raiseroom/app && flock -n /var/lock/raiseroom-backup.lock docker compose exec -T app node tools/backup.mjs --data-dir /data --dest /backups --retain-days 35 2>&1 | logger -t raiseroom-backup

# ── health, degraded storage and disk, every minute ────────────────────────
# Against the PUBLIC url, deliberately: a check against loopback passes while
# TLS is expired and while DNS points at somebody else.
* * * * * cd /srv/raiseroom/app && flock -n /var/lock/raiseroom-watch.lock node --experimental-sqlite tools/watch.mjs --url https://raiseroom.app --data-dir /srv/raiseroom/data --state /var/lib/raiseroom/watch-state.json 2>&1 | logger -t raiseroom-watch

# ── optional: prune usage counters over 24 months old ──────────────────────
# The application does this once per process as a safety net, so a host that
# restarts occasionally does not need this line at all. See docs/DEPLOY.md.
# 30 3 * * 0 cd /srv/raiseroom/app && docker compose exec -T app node tools/usage.mjs --prune 2>&1 | logger -t raiseroom-usage
